# Accepted residual CVEs. Every entry documents why it is accepted and when to
# remove it. The Trivy gate in the release flow must pass with ONLY these
# suppressions -- a new finding means a new decision, not a new entry by reflex.
#
# SCOPE: this file holds Debian trixie base CVEs that appear in ALL THREE images
# (app, tts, render). Image-specific acceptances live in .trivyignore.tts and
# .trivyignore.render; scripts/trivy_gate.sh concatenates the appropriate pair
# before passing --ignorefile to each trivy invocation. This eliminates the
# global-masking problem where a single ignorefile silently suppresses CVEs
# across images that do not trigger them.

# -- Debian trixie base (python:*-slim): no fixed package released yet.
# Remove each when `apt-get upgrade` in a rebuild clears it from the scan.

# perl / perl-base / libperl5.40 / perl-modules-5.40 (CRITICAL x3, HIGH x4):
# interpreter ships in the slim base; nothing in Audicle invokes perl.
# Statuses: CVE-2026-8376, CVE-2026-48962, CVE-2026-13221 and CVE-2026-57432
# are "affected"; the other three are "fix_deferred". All seven are equally
# not-yet-fixed in trixie.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-9538
# regex engine silently-incorrect-match (CRITICAL) and S_measure_struct integer
# overflow (HIGH), added 0.48.2:
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-57432

# curl / libcurl4t64 / libcurl3t64-gnutls (HIGH x10):
# system curl ships in base; backend Python httpx does not use system libcurl.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-5773
CVE-2026-6276
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8927
CVE-2026-8932
CVE-2026-9079
CVE-2026-9080
CVE-2026-9545
CVE-2026-9547

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) (HIGH x1):
# terminal handling in base; Audicle runs headless in a container.
CVE-2025-69720

# gzip (HIGH x1): compression utility in base; not invoked by application code.
CVE-2026-41992

# util-linux family (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1,
# libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux) (HIGH x1):
# standard system utilities in the slim base; not exposed to untrusted input.
CVE-2026-53615

# libacl1 (HIGH x1): POSIX ACL library in base; no ACL operations in Audicle.
CVE-2026-54369

# libsndfile1 (HIGH x1): audio file library in the Debian base;
# Audicle uses soundfile (Python binding) for read/write only, no untrusted files.
# Present in app and tts images; included here so the app scan (shared-only) passes.
CVE-2026-37555

# perl Storable (perl-base in app/render; libperl5.40, perl, perl-base,
# perl-modules-5.40 in tts) (CRITICAL x1, "affected"): signed integer overflow
# in Storable before 3.41 (CVE-2026-57433). Perl rides in the Debian base;
# no application code invokes perl or deserializes Storable data. No Debian
# fix released. Added 0.48.3. Remove when trixie ships a patched perl.
CVE-2026-57433

# CVE-2026-8458 (curl/libcurl, HIGH): unauthorized connection reuse. No fixed
# package exists in Debian trixie as of 2026-08-10 (trivy status: affected,
# empty fixed-version). Present in all three images, which is why it lives in
# the shared file: each installs curl solely for the localhost container
# healthcheck; article fetching uses httpx, never libcurl. Re-check each
# release and drop this entry when deb13u ships a fixed curl.
CVE-2026-8458

# CVE-2026-58050 (libssh2-1t64, HIGH): heap buffer overflow via integer
# overflow in publickey attribute allocation. No fixed package in Debian trixie
# as of 2026-08-11 (trivy status: affected, empty fixed-version). Present in all
# three images as a transitive dependency of libcurl4t64, which is installed
# only for the localhost healthcheck. The bug sits in libssh2's SSH
# authentication path, reachable only through an scp:// or sftp:// transfer;
# no image ships git or ssh, and the HTTP stack is httpx, never libcurl.
# Re-check each release and drop this entry when deb13u ships a fixed libssh2.
CVE-2026-58050
